---
// Literal recreation of the Claude Design canvas's Admin Ticket Detail
// screen (project/AdminTicketDetail.dc.html -> NavSidebar role="admin"
// active="Support tickets" + the shared NavTop.astro (section="Manage"
// parent="Support tickets" page=<real ticket id, sliced>) + PageAdminTicket
// -> this is the dedicated ADMIN ticket-detail artboard (thread + composer
// on the left, Details/Status/Assignee/"Customer's other tickets" cards on
// the right, header quick-actions "Mark resolved"/"Close ticket"). No
// markup reused from Customer Support Ticket or Inventory Staff Support
// Ticket (a genuinely different split-pane artboard, PageTickets.dc.html) —
// this file owns its own full markup/CSS, same convention as every other
// screen in this project.
//
// ROUTE: /admin/tickets/[id] (new this turn). /admin/tickets' rows now link
// here (see that file's own updated header comment).
//
// SCHEMA REALITY vs THE DESIGN — support_tickets has exactly nine real
// columns (id, created_by, assigned_to, subject, description, status,
// resolution, created_at, updated_at, confirmed live). No
// support_ticket_messages/attachments/category/order_id/SLA/assignment-
// history/internal-notes table exists anywhere in this schema. Every
// fabricated element the design shows for TK-1191 (a multi-turn customer/
// staff/internal-note conversation, "Order issue" category, a related
// order SO-10482, an assignee-reassignment dropdown, a company name +
// "C-2041" customer code) was checked against the real schema and handled
// as follows — never invented:
//  - Conversation thread: replaced with the two pieces of real text this
//    ticket actually has — the original report (ticket.description,
//    always present) and, once set, the resolution notes
//    (ticket.resolution) — same "real opening description + real
//    resolution only when it exists" precedent already used on Inventory
//    Staff's own ticket detail page. An honest banner discloses that no
//    real message thread exists. The design's composer is reproduced
//    visually (textarea + Attach + Send, same layout) but fully disabled
//    with explanatory titles — never pretends a reply/attachment write
//    path exists. The design's dual "Reply to customer"/"Internal note"
//    tabs were dropped rather than reproduced-and-disabled: neither a
//    message table nor an internal-notes table exists, so implying two
//    distinct real capabilities would itself be a fabrication.
//  - Category ("Order issue") and "Related order" (SO-10482): both fully
//    omitted from the Details card — support_tickets has no category or
//    order_id column at all, not even an untracked-but-real concept (unlike
//    e.g. a physical bin location), so there is nothing honest to display
//    even as "—". Same "wholly nonexistent concept -> full omission"
//    precedent already used for Category on Admin Products/Product Info.
//  - Company name ("Meera Traders") + customer code ("C-2041"): customers
//    has no company/name/code column (confirmed against
//    0002_profiles_customers.sql — id, profile_id, billing_address,
//    shipping_address, notes, marketing_opt_in only). The requester is
//    shown by their real profiles.full_name only, with the same real
//    Customer vs "Internal · {name}" distinction already used on the
//    ticket queue, never a fabricated company/code.
//  - Assignment control: inspected updateSupportTicket (src/actions/
//    index.ts) before building anything — it only ever writes
//    status/resolution, never assigned_to, even though
//    support_tickets_update_admin's RLS would technically permit admin to
//    write assigned_to via a raw table update. No Action/RPC exists that
//    does so. Per your explicit fallback ("display the real assignee, omit
//    or disable the assignment control honestly"), the Assignee card is
//    real but non-interactive — shows the real assignee name + role or
//    "Unassigned", with an honest disabled-control affordance and a title
//    explaining why, matching the same disabled-control convention used
//    for the "+ Category" facet on the ticket queue. No STOP was needed —
//    your own instructions supply this exact honest fallback.
//  - "Customer's other tickets": real and functional — other real
//    support_tickets rows sharing this ticket's real created_by, each
//    linking to this same new /admin/tickets/[id] route (a real link to a
//    screen that now exists, not a forward reference to an unbuilt one).
//
// FUNCTIONALITY — the one real mutation path: reuses updateSupportTicket
// exactly as shipped (status + resolution only). The Status card's real
// <select> (all 5 real ticket_status values) + resolution textarea + Save
// button submit it directly. The header's "Mark resolved"/"Close ticket"
// quick-actions are not a second system — they set the same select's value
// and submit the same one form/action (hidden once their target status is
// already current, so there's no redundant no-op button). Same
// submit/redirect-with-?updated=1/banner pattern already used on the
// Inventory Staff ticket page, reproduced here (not copy-pasted — this
// file's markup/CSS is entirely its own).
//
// PRESERVED UNCHANGED: support_tickets schema/RLS, Customer Support,
// Customer Support Ticket, Inventory Staff Support (its own
// updateSupportTicket usage untouched), every other already-approved Admin
// screen. Admin Team/Reports/Settings not implemented.
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import NavSidebar from "../../../components/staff/NavSidebar.astro";
import NavTop from "../../../components/staff/NavTop.astro";

const { id } = Astro.params;
const url = Astro.url;
const updated = url.searchParams.get("updated");
const viewerRole = (Astro.locals.role === "super_admin" ? "super_admin" : "admin") as "admin" | "super_admin";

// --- Real ticket (support_tickets_select_admin — unscoped, admin/super_admin see every ticket) ---
const { data: ticket } = await Astro.locals.supabase
  .from("support_tickets")
  .select("id, subject, description, status, resolution, created_by, assigned_to, created_at, updated_at")
  .eq("id", id)
  .maybeSingle();

if (!ticket) {
  Astro.response.status = 404;
}

const STATUS_LABEL: Record<string, string> = {
  open: "Open",
  in_progress: "In Progress",
  waiting: "Waiting",
  resolved: "Resolved",
  closed: "Closed",
};
const STATUS_TONE: Record<string, "outline" | "info" | "warn" | "success" | "muted"> = {
  open: "outline",
  in_progress: "info",
  waiting: "warn",
  resolved: "success",
  closed: "muted",
};
const ALL_STATUSES = ["open", "in_progress", "waiting", "resolved", "closed"] as const;
const ROLE_LABEL: Record<string, string> = {
  customer: "Customer",
  sales_staff: "Sales staff",
  inventory_staff: "Inventory staff",
  admin: "Admin",
  super_admin: "Super admin",
};

// --- Real requester/assignee profiles ---
const relevantProfileIds = ticket ? [...new Set([ticket.created_by, ticket.assigned_to].filter((v): v is string => Boolean(v)))] : [];
const { data: profileRows } =
  relevantProfileIds.length > 0 ? await Astro.locals.supabase.from("profiles").select("id, full_name, role").in("id", relevantProfileIds) : { data: [] };
const profileById = new Map((profileRows ?? []).map((p) => [p.id, { name: p.full_name ?? "Unnamed", role: p.role as string }]));

const creator = ticket ? profileById.get(ticket.created_by) : undefined;
const isInternalCreator = creator ? creator.role !== "customer" : false;
const requesterName = creator?.name ?? "—";
const requesterRoleLabel = creator ? (ROLE_LABEL[creator.role] ?? creator.role) : "—";
const assigneeProfile = ticket?.assigned_to ? profileById.get(ticket.assigned_to) : undefined;

// --- Real "other tickets from this requester" (support_tickets_select_admin — unscoped) ---
const { data: otherTicketRows } = ticket
  ? await Astro.locals.supabase
      .from("support_tickets")
      .select("id, subject, status, updated_at")
      .eq("created_by", ticket.created_by)
      .neq("id", ticket.id)
      .order("updated_at", { ascending: false })
      .limit(5)
  : { data: [] };
const otherTickets = otherTicketRows ?? [];

function initials(name: string): string {
  const parts = name.split(" ").filter(Boolean).slice(0, 2).map((p) => p[0]!.toUpperCase());
  return parts.length > 0 ? parts.join("") : "—";
}
function fmtDateTime(iso: string): string {
  return new Date(iso).toLocaleString(undefined, { day: "numeric", month: "short", year: "numeric", hour: "numeric", minute: "2-digit" });
}
---

<BaseLayout title={ticket ? `${ticket.subject} — Support` : "Ticket not found — Support"}>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" />
  </Fragment>

  <div class="sd" id="sd-root">
    <div id="sd-sidebar-backdrop" class="sd__backdrop"></div>

    <div id="sd-sidebar" class="sd__sidebar">
      <NavSidebar active="Support tickets" role="admin" viewerRole={viewerRole} />
    </div>

    <div class="sd__panel">
      <NavTop section="Manage" parent="Support tickets" page={ticket ? ticket.id.slice(0, 8) : "Not found"} />

      <main id="main-content" class="tkd__main">
        {
          ticket ? (
            <Fragment>
              <a href="/admin/tickets" class="tkd__back">
                <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m15 18-6-6 6-6" /></svg>
                Support tickets
              </a>

              {updated && (
                <p class="tkd__banner" role="status">
                  Ticket updated.
                </p>
              )}

              <div class="tkd__title-row">
                <div class="tkd__title-col">
                  <div class="tkd__title-top">
                    <h1>{ticket.subject}</h1>
                    <span class={`tk__pill tk__pill--${STATUS_TONE[ticket.status] ?? "muted"}`}>{STATUS_LABEL[ticket.status] ?? ticket.status}</span>
                  </div>
                  <span class="tkd__meta">
                    {ticket.id.slice(0, 8)} · {isInternalCreator ? `Internal · ${requesterName}` : requesterName} · opened {fmtDateTime(ticket.created_at as string)}
                  </span>
                </div>
                <div class="tkd__quick-actions">
                  {ticket.status !== "resolved" && ticket.status !== "closed" && (
                    <button type="button" id="tkd-quick-resolve" class="tk__btn">
                      <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5" /></svg>
                      Mark resolved
                    </button>
                  )}
                  {ticket.status !== "closed" && (
                    <button type="button" id="tkd-quick-close" class="tk__btn">
                      <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6 6 18" /></svg>
                      Close ticket
                    </button>
                  )}
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="tkd__body">
                <section aria-label="Ticket thread" class="tkd__thread-panel">
                  <div class="tkd__thread-scroll">
                    <article class="tkd__msg">
                      <span class="tkd__avatar">{initials(requesterName)}</span>
                      <div class="tkd__msg-body">
                        <div class="tkd__msg-head">
                          <span class="tkd__msg-name">{requesterName}</span>
                          <span class="tkd__msg-role">{isInternalCreator ? `Internal · ${requesterRoleLabel}` : "Customer"}</span>
                          <span class="tkd__msg-time">{fmtDateTime(ticket.created_at as string)}</span>
                        </div>
                        <p class="tkd__msg-text">{ticket.description}</p>
                      </div>
                    </article>
                    {ticket.resolution && (
                      <article class="tkd__msg tkd__msg--resolution">
                        <span class="tkd__avatar tkd__avatar--resolution">
                          <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 11h12v10H6zM8 11V7a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v4" /></svg>
                        </span>
                        <div class="tkd__msg-body">
                          <div class="tkd__msg-head">
                            <span class="tkd__msg-name">Resolution notes</span>
                            <span class="tkd__msg-time">{fmtDateTime(ticket.updated_at as string)}</span>
                          </div>
                          <p class="tkd__msg-text">{ticket.resolution}</p>
                        </div>
                      </article>
                    )}
                  </div>
                  <div class="tkd__thread-banner">There’s no message thread in this system yet — Status on the right is the real way to update this ticket.</div>
                  <div class="tkd__composer" aria-disabled="true">
                    <textarea disabled placeholder="Replying isn’t available in this system yet" />
                    <div class="tkd__composer-actions">
                      <button type="button" class="tk__btn" disabled title="Attachments aren’t available in this system yet">
                        <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M21 11.5 12.5 20a5 5 0 0 1-7-7L14 4.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 5 5L10.5 18a2 2 0 0 1-3-3L15 7.5" /></svg>
                        Attach
                      </button>
                      <div class="tkd__spacer" />
                      <button type="button" class="tk__btn tk__btn--primary" disabled title="Replying isn’t available in this system yet">
                        <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 12 20 4l-6 16-3-7z" /></svg>
                        Send
                      </button>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </section>

                <div class="tkd__side">
                  <section aria-label="Details" class="tkd__card">
                    <h2>Details</h2>
                    <div class="tkd__requester-row">
                      <span class="tkd__avatar">{initials(requesterName)}</span>
                      <span class="tkd__requester-col">
                        <span class="tkd__requester-name">{requesterName}</span>
                        <span class="tkd__requester-role">{isInternalCreator ? `Internal · ${requesterRoleLabel}` : "Customer"}</span>
                      </span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="tkd__kv">
                      <span>Created</span>
                      <span>{fmtDateTime(ticket.created_at as string)}</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="tkd__kv">
                      <span>Updated</span>
                      <span>{fmtDateTime(ticket.updated_at as string)}</span>
                    </div>
                  </section>

                  <section aria-label="Status" class="tkd__card">
                    <h2>Status</h2>
                    <form id="tkd-update-form" class="tkd__update-form">
                      <input type="hidden" name="ticketId" value={ticket.id} />
                      <select id="tkd-status" name="status" aria-label="Status">
                        {ALL_STATUSES.map((s) => (
                          <option value={s} selected={ticket.status === s}>{STATUS_LABEL[s]}</option>
                        ))}
                      </select>
                      <textarea id="tkd-resolution" name="resolution" class="tkd__resolution" aria-label="Resolution notes" placeholder="Resolution notes (visible to the requester)">{ticket.resolution ?? ""}</textarea>
                      <p id="tkd-form-message" class="tkd__form-message" role="status" />
                      <button type="submit" class="tk__btn tk__btn--primary">Save</button>
                    </form>
                  </section>

                  <section aria-label="Assignee" class="tkd__card">
                    <h2>Assignee</h2>
                    <div class="tkd__assignee-row" title="Assigning tickets isn’t available in this system yet">
                      {assigneeProfile ? (
                        <Fragment>
                          <span class="tkd__avatar">{initials(assigneeProfile.name)}</span>
                          <span class="tkd__requester-col">
                            <span class="tkd__requester-name">{assigneeProfile.name}</span>
                            <span class="tkd__requester-role">{ROLE_LABEL[assigneeProfile.role] ?? assigneeProfile.role}</span>
                          </span>
                        </Fragment>
                      ) : (
                        <span class="tkd__muted">Unassigned</span>
                      )}
                    </div>
                    <span class="tkd__hint">Assigning tickets isn’t available in this system yet.</span>
                  </section>

                  <section aria-label="Requester's other tickets" class="tkd__card">
                    <h2>{isInternalCreator ? "Other tickets from this requester" : "Customer’s other tickets"}</h2>
                    {otherTickets.length > 0 ? (
                      otherTickets.map((o) => (
                        <a href={`/admin/tickets/${o.id}`} class="tkd__other-row">
                          <span class="tkd__other-subject">{o.subject}</span>
                          <span class={`tk__pill tk__pill--${STATUS_TONE[o.status as string] ?? "muted"}`}>{STATUS_LABEL[o.status as string] ?? o.status}</span>
                        </a>
                      ))
                    ) : (
                      <p class="tkd__muted tkd__muted--block">No other tickets from this requester.</p>
                    )}
                  </section>
                </div>
              </div>
            </Fragment>
          ) : (
            <div class="tkd__empty">
              <p class="tkd__empty-title">Ticket not found</p>
              <p class="tkd__empty-body">It may have been removed, or the link may be wrong.</p>
              <a href="/admin/tickets" class="tk__btn">Back to Support tickets</a>
            </div>
          )
        }
      </main>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .sd {
    --sd-shell: #fafafa;
    --sd-panel: #ffffff;
    --sd-card: #ffffff;
    --sd-fg: #0a0a0a;
    --sd-fg2: #404040;
    --sd-muted: #f5f5f5;
    --sd-muted-fg: #737373;
    --sd-border: #e5e5e5;
    --sd-input: #e5e5e5;
    --sd-primary: #171717;
    --sd-primary-fg: #fafafa;
    --sd-success-bg: #ecfdf3;
    --sd-success-fg: #15803d;
    --sd-warn-bg: #fef3e2;
    --sd-warn-fg: #9a3412;
    --sd-danger-bg: #feecec;
    --sd-danger-fg: #b91c1c;
    --sd-info-bg: #eef2ff;
    --sd-info-fg: #3538cd;
    --sd-accent: #2b50e0;
    --sd-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);
    color-scheme: light;

    min-height: 100vh;
    display: flex;
    background: var(--sd-shell);
    color: var(--sd-fg);
    font-family: "Geist", system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .sd[data-theme="dark"] {
    --sd-shell: #0a0a0a;
    --sd-panel: #0f0f0f;
    --sd-card: #171717;
    --sd-fg: #fafafa;
    --sd-fg2: #d4d4d4;
    --sd-muted: #262626;
    --sd-muted-fg: #a3a3a3;
    --sd-border: #262626;
    --sd-input: #363636;
    --sd-primary: #fafafa;
    --sd-primary-fg: #171717;
    --sd-success-bg: #0f2a1c;
    --sd-success-fg: #4ade80;
    --sd-warn-bg: #2e1f0e;
    --sd-warn-fg: #fdba74;
    --sd-danger-bg: #2d1414;
    --sd-danger-fg: #f87171;
    --sd-info-bg: #1e2240;
    --sd-info-fg: #a5b4fc;
    --sd-accent: #6b8afb;
    --sd-shadow: none;
    color-scheme: dark;
  }
  .sd__backdrop {
    display: none;
    position: fixed;
    inset: 0;
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4);
    z-index: 20;
  }
  .sd__sidebar {
    height: 100vh;
    position: sticky;
    top: 0;
  }
  @media (max-width: 1023px) {
    .sd__sidebar {
      position: fixed;
      top: 0;
      left: 0;
      bottom: 0;
      z-index: 30;
      transform: translateX(-100%);
      transition: transform 0.2s ease;
    }
    .sd__sidebar.is-open {
      transform: translateX(0);
    }
    .sd__backdrop.is-open {
      display: block;
    }
  }
  .sd__panel {
    flex-grow: 1;
    min-width: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    margin: 8px 8px 8px 0;
    background: var(--sd-panel);
    border: 1px solid var(--sd-border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: var(--sd-shadow);
  }
  @media (max-width: 1023px) {
    .sd__panel {
      margin: 8px;
    }
  }

  .tkd__main {
    flex-grow: 1;
    min-height: 0;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    padding: 24px 32px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .tkd__main {
      padding: 16px;
    }
  }

  .tkd__back {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-self: flex-start;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 4px;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--sd-muted-fg);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .tkd__banner {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--sd-success-fg);
  }

  .tkd__title-row {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: flex-end;
    gap: 16px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .tkd__title-col {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .tkd__title-top {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .tkd__title-top h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 22px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .tkd__meta {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--sd-muted-fg);
  }
  .tkd__quick-actions {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .tk__btn {
    height: 36px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    padding: 0 14px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    border: 1px solid var(--sd-input);
    background: var(--sd-card);
    color: var(--sd-fg);
    font: inherit;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .tk__btn:disabled {
    cursor: not-allowed;
    opacity: 0.55;
  }
  .tk__btn--primary {
    border: 0;
    background: var(--sd-primary);
    color: var(--sd-primary-fg);
  }

  .tk__pill {
    padding: 2px 8px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 500;
    white-space: nowrap;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .tk__pill--outline {
    border: 1px solid var(--sd-input);
    color: var(--sd-fg);
  }
  .tk__pill--info {
    background: var(--sd-info-bg);
    color: var(--sd-info-fg);
  }
  .tk__pill--warn {
    background: var(--sd-warn-bg);
    color: var(--sd-warn-fg);
  }
  .tk__pill--success {
    background: var(--sd-success-bg);
    color: var(--sd-success-fg);
  }
  .tk__pill--muted {
    background: var(--sd-muted);
    color: var(--sd-muted-fg);
  }

  .tkd__body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
    min-height: 0;
  }
  @media (min-width: 1050px) {
    .tkd__body {
      flex-direction: row;
      align-items: flex-start;
    }
  }

  .tkd__thread-panel {
    flex-grow: 1;
    min-width: 0;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    border: 1px solid var(--sd-border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--sd-card);
    box-shadow: var(--sd-shadow);
    overflow: hidden;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }
  .tkd__thread-scroll {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    padding: 14px 16px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
    background: var(--sd-shell);
    max-height: 420px;
    overflow-y: auto;
  }
  .tkd__msg {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    padding: 12px 14px;
    border: 1px solid var(--sd-border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--sd-card);
    display: flex;
